Follow-up to the rail commit (fahreza wanted rail and swipe as separate commits). No backend work - /v1/android/swipe was added earlier (5cfe917 area). Replaced the img onclick=handleClick with onpointerdown/onpointerup: pressStart records start point (device px) + Date.now(); on up, Math.hypot(dx,dy) < SWIPE_THRESHOLD(12 device px) => tap (preserves old behavior), else => swipe with ms = clamp(elapsed,50,800) so a flick is fast and a deliberate drag is slow. setPointerCapture on down so pointerup fires even if released outside the image; touch-none prevents the browser eating the gesture on touch, select-none stops drag-selecting the img. Date.now() is fine here (browser code, not the Workflow sandbox). Frame refreshes mid-drag don't matter - same <img>, stable getBoundingClientRect. NOT yet rebuilt into the installer at commit time.
